(7031440, 1066528, 69008, '<td valign="top">Hi Lizzie!  It''s too bad this one got DQ''d, since it''s your first entry here at DPC.  I am guessing that the date in your camera was not set, so the exif file shows a date different from the actual shooting date.  It''s a common mistake, so it''s not a big deal. I think that probably over half of all the DPC''ers have at least one DQ. <br/> <br/>About the photo, most of the photos of little critters that do well in the challenges are shot tight or cropped so that the critter is filling most of the frame, unless there is something else in the image that''s supporting the focus on the critter.  An example of that would be keeping part of a twig or flower that a butterfly or dragonfly is sitting on, as a "leading line" to give the image some dynamic impact. <br/> <br/>Anyway, welcome to DPC.  You got off to a rough start here, but hopefully you will stick around to learn more about photography, and to and meet some people here.  The side challenges are great for that.</td>', 'Hi Lizzie!  It''s too bad this one got DQ''d, since it''s your first entry here at DPC.  I am guessing that the date in your camera was not set, so the exif file shows a date different from the actual shooting date.  It''s a common mistake, so it''s not a big deal. I think that probably over half of all the DPC''ers have at least one DQ.  About the photo, most of the photos of little critters that do well in the challenges are shot tight or cropped so that the critter is filling most of the frame, unless there is something else in the image that''s supporting the focus on the critter.  An example of that would be keeping part of a twig or flower that a butterfly or dragonfly is sitting on, as a "leading line" to give the image some dynamic impact.  Anyway, welcome to DPC.  You got off to a rough start here, but hopefully you will stick around to learn more about photography, and to and meet some people here.  The side challenges are great for that.', '2013-05-03 10:19:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7031562, 1066685, 62318, '<td valign="top">I like the choice of the pink on pink, it really separates it from other images with a similar setup. Wonderfully rendered.</td>', 'I like the choice of the pink on pink, it really separates it from other images with a similar setup. Wonderfully rendered.', '2013-05-03 12:53:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7031592, 1066650, 109341, '<td valign="top">Nicely balanced!  Great shot, congrats!</td>', 'Nicely balanced!  Great shot, congrats!', '2013-05-03 13:28:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7032056, 1066503, 31456, '<td valign="top">Thank you to all the voters and commenters! I don''t have a lot of experience with macro photography, so you <b>know</b> I''m overjoyed with how well it did, and with such praise from <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=52549" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">IreneM</a>. This was one of maybe 20-30 shots of just this bee (itself one of many that I chased around), and really the only one that was in focus and had an acceptable amount of motion blur (there is some visible at 100%). The composition was mostly achieved through cropping, since I had little time to compose while shooting.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-01-31 00:07:08.</i></td>', 'Thank you to all the voters and commenters! I don''t have a lot of experience with macro photography, so you know I''m overjoyed with how well it did, and with such praise from  IreneM. This was one of maybe 20-30 shots of just this bee (itself one of many that I chased around), and really the only one that was in focus and had an acceptable amount of motion blur (there is some visible at 100%). The composition was mostly achieved through cropping, since I had little time to compose while shooting.', '2013-05-04 19:17:49.000000', '2014-01-31 00:07:08.000000', 0),
(7032059, 1066650, 31456, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the blue!! This was one of my favorite shots from the challenge, fresh and crisp :)</td>', 'Congrats on the blue!! This was one of my favorite shots from the challenge, fresh and crisp :)', '2013-05-04 19:23:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7032061, 1066374, 31456, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the finish! How fitting that two of the three on the podium would be tulip shots :).<br/> <br/>I think you should''ve gotten the red, though - your shot is superior to mine, both photographically and in terms of processing.</td>', 'Congrats on the finish! How fitting that two of the three on the podium would be tulip shots :). I think you should''ve gotten the red, though - your shot is superior to mine, both photographically and in terms of processing.', '2013-05-04 19:37:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7032062, 1066134, 31456, '<td valign="top">By far my favorite shot this challenge. My only 10.</td>', 'By far my favorite shot this challenge. My only 10.', '2013-05-04 19:44:49.000000', NULL, 0),
